WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
- A long time ago, but not long enough ago

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.292
that it's not still very relevant

00:00:05.292 --> 00:00:06.770
(audience laughs)

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.750
everyone in Britain got in a big old boat,

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.540
and we set sail and we robbed,

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.080
and this will sound far-fetched,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.582
everyone in the world.

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:14.636
(audience laughs)

00:00:14.636 --> 00:00:15.469
Do you remember that?

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:16.302
What a spree that was?

00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:17.135
Do you remember the great heist?

00:00:17.135 --> 00:00:18.371
What a spree.

00:00:18.371 --> 00:00:21.220
(audience laughs)

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.277
And we got all this swag didn't we?

00:00:22.277 --> 00:00:24.130
And we took it back to old blighty

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.840
and we hid it, this is the clever part,

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.331
we hid it in a museum.

00:00:28.331 --> 00:00:31.164
(audience laughs)

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.183
Last place anyone looks.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.140
Now it's the modern day,

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.290
and all them countries we stole stuff from

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.370
are asking for their stuff back.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:41.930
But don't be worried.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:44.291
We're totally saying a blanket no.

00:00:44.291 --> 00:00:47.124
(audience laughs)

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.460
Now, a few of you are sitting there,

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.660
I can see your angry faces,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.342
like "So what? Finders keepers, shut up."

00:00:54.342 --> 00:00:57.443
And--
(audience laughs)

00:00:57.443 --> 00:01:00.050
listen, in your defense,
"finders keepers, shut up"

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.818
has worked very well for us so far.

00:01:02.818 --> 00:01:04.247
Gents does and knocked it out of the park

00:01:04.247 --> 00:01:05.627
"finders keepers, shut up".

00:01:08.713 --> 00:01:10.040
But even you got to admit, right,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.290
if someone stole something
off you as an individual,

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:13.740
it was your favorite
thing and they nicked it,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.500
and you knew who had nicked it by the way

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.720
for a fact, not a hunch,
you know who's stolen it.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.640
Everybody knows, it's common knowledge.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.100
Some people have written books about it.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.699
They have definitely nicked it off you.

00:01:24.699 --> 00:01:26.357
(audience laughs)

00:01:26.357 --> 00:01:28.360
You go to ask for it back,
and they just standing there.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:29.535
They're not even running away.

00:01:29.535 --> 00:01:30.770
And they're twice your
size, they ain't scared.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.150
They haven't even bothered to hide it.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.800
They've done the opposite
of hiding it actually.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.824
They put it in a glass display case.

00:01:35.824 --> 00:01:36.990
(audience laughs)

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.810
It's lit from seven different
angles, real clear what it is.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.010
There's no disputing it's the same thing

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.010
that once belonged to you cause
there's a plaque next to it,

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.750
says exactly what it is
at the top of the plaque,

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.020
and then a paragraph underneath

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.506
about how important it is
to you and your culture.

00:01:50.506 --> 00:01:53.339
(audience laughs)

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.497
You'd be forgiven for
thinking, "Mmm I'm pretty sure

00:01:57.497 --> 00:01:59.260
"they haven't got a leg to stand on here.

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:00.107
(audience laughs)

00:02:00.107 --> 00:02:02.560
"Probably gonna take this home today."

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.170
Must have been so confident,
all them countries

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.590
when they asked for their stuffs back.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.197
Walking up to Britain,
saying to their friends,

00:02:07.197 --> 00:02:09.846
"Wait in the car, don't even need ya.

00:02:09.846 --> 00:02:11.273
"Be back in a jiffy mate.

00:02:14.047 --> 00:02:16.817
"Hey man, a while ago,
a lot of your ancestors

00:02:16.817 --> 00:02:18.547
"stole loads of stuff from my ancestors.

00:02:18.547 --> 00:02:20.487
"Yeah, I'm here to take them home.

00:02:20.487 --> 00:02:23.505
"Let's right this wrong, what do you say?"

00:02:23.505 --> 00:02:25.700
They must have thought the
British person at the door

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.177
was gonna go, "Absolutely
you can have them back.

00:02:29.177 --> 00:02:30.967
"We stole them after all."

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:36.547
But instead we went, "I don't think so.

00:02:36.547 --> 00:02:37.777
(audience laughs)

00:02:37.777 --> 00:02:39.532
"We're still looking at it.

00:02:39.532 --> 00:02:43.282
(audience laughs and cheers)

00:02:48.987 --> 00:02:51.177
"Yeah, just looking at it these days.

00:02:51.177 --> 00:02:52.877
"And there's a lot of other
people who haven't seen it yet

00:02:52.877 --> 00:02:54.237
"we'd quite like to show it to.

00:02:54.237 --> 00:02:56.792
"So not right now selfish.

00:02:56.792 --> 00:03:00.007
(audience laughs)

00:03:00.007 --> 00:03:00.840
"Don't sulk about it.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.047
"Look, it's no hard feelings mate.

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:03.577
"Hey, you can look at it, come on in.

00:03:03.577 --> 00:03:04.967
"Have a look; have a look.

00:03:04.967 --> 00:03:06.045
"Seem familiar?

00:03:06.045 --> 00:03:08.857
(evil chortle)

00:03:08.857 --> 00:03:10.663
"Stand behind the rope!"

00:03:10.663 --> 00:03:13.714
(audience laughs)

00:03:13.714 --> 00:03:15.600
That's why the British Museum
is so busy all the time.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.940
No British people ever go in there,

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.101
it's full of people from abroad
looking at their own stuff.

00:03:19.101 --> 00:03:21.200
(audience laughs)

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.310
Just walking the corridors,

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:24.080
reminiscing about the good old days.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.710
And I imagine just openly
robbing the gift shop at the end.

00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:29.113
That is one all you punks.

